WEBVTT

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.770
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.020
<i>Jean and the rest escaped from the
island base of Neo Atlantis.</i>

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:33.400
<i>They were rescued by the Nautilus,
and permitted to go on board.</i>

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.610
<i>Jean and Hanson are overjoyed for
the opportunity to stay on a ship</i>

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>filled with the products
of future science.</i>

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.330
<i>Grandis encounters Captain Nemo,
and falls in love at first sight.</i>

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.490
<i>On the Nautilus, Captain Nemo
is introduced to Nadia,</i>

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.080
<i>He is shocked to see her Blue Water,
and realizes her identity.</i>

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>What is the mysterious secret that
lies within the Blue Water?</i>

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.900
Then, you knew about Nadia.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.270
Yes, Sir.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:13.820
I see.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:17.280
However, it's none of my business.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.370
That's true. You may go.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.320
Yes, Sir.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.170
I'm afraid. Why?

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.050
Sorry if I woke you up.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.470
What's the matter?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.970
Nothing for you to worry about.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.890
What's all the fuss about?
Can't you be more quiet?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.020
What an obnoxious person!

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.770
Men are so useless!

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.030
Chief Engineer to the bridge.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:10.000
Repairs on the main engines are
complete. Ready for test dive.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.250
Roger, thank you.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.460
Good morning, Captain Nemo.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.130
Morning.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.920
Everything is progressing on schedule.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.090
Sea trials should commence
in about five minutes.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.050
First Officer...

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:25.680
Yes, Sir.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.180
About our passengers...

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:29.890
Yes?

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:32.350
You can't mean that!

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.820
It can't be helped. Captain's orders.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.320
The captain's?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.200
But you'll be able to visit Nadia
any time you want.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.700
Nothing has really changed.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.870
Yes, it has! A lot!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.540
Why? Tell me why!

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.750
I guess it's because you
are grown-ups now.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.340
A mature man and woman
sharing the same room

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.970
may create a problem.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.260
That's what he was worried about.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.390
Jean, how could you?! Horrible!

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.400
You're horrible!

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.320
No, you've got me all wrong!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:18.440
Get out!

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.070
Nadia...

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:25.410
I hate you! I hate everyone!
I hate everything!

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:35.210
Hey, Hanson, why did they transfer
Jean into our room all of a sudden?

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:35.790
Dunno.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.380
To keep an eye on us?

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.000
Dunno.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.920
It's hard to think of Jean
acting as a spy.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:43.760
Dunno.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:48.300
Anyway, the quicker we get away
from this ship, the better.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.270
I'd like stay on board a
little while longer.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.520
Don't you care if Nemo steals
Grandis away from us?!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.060
If you put it that way...

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:03.190
Hey, Nadia, why did you get
so mad at Jean?

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.360
I really don't know.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.990
Grown-ups are so hard to figure out.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.160
I'm not a grown-up yet.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.750
But that scary lady said you
were both adults.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.420
We're not adults yet.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.340
We're still children.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:32.720
You're a man, aren't you?
Show some spirit, Jean.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.190
It's so hard when the other person
doesn't realize how much you care.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:40.900
Especially when you're on the same
ship, and can't meet each other.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:47.860
Then when you do meet, you
find yourself speechless.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:50.580
Is that the way it is?

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:58.370
But when repairs are completed on my
Katherine, we'll have to leave.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.460
Seniorita, repairs are complete.
We can leave anytime.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.410
Goodbye, Mama! Papa!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:32.740
You don't have to say goodbye, Marie.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.370
They're always watching
you from the sky.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.080
What about your mama and papa?

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.960
That's true.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.550
They're probably up there too with
your mama and papa.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.130
Then, they're all together!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:50.970
Captain Nemo...

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.220
I detect something approaching
from the air, 5 o'clock astern.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:54.930
What distance?

00:06:55.390 --> 00:07:00.390
About twelve kilometers and closing.
Speed twenty-seven knots.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.020
It's probably Gargoyle's airship.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.980
I wonder why it has come
back this way?

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.280
Could be a trap.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:15.240
King, I wonder if Africa lies
beyond those clouds.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.460
What can that be?

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.920
It's headed northeast.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.380
Shall we track it down?

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:32.760
Helmsman, make a 180 degree turn,
and prepare to submerge!

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:34.100
Roger!

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.310
Prepare to submerge!
Prepare to submerge!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:39.730
When we get close, slow down.
We'll follow at the same speed.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.940
The airship is headed for
the Le Mer Straits.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.940
Hey, didn't you hear the orders?!
We're going to crash dive!

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.150
You want to drown?

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:49.530
Right!

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.360
What is it? What's happening?

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.490
Top deck all clear!

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.490
All stations ready for submerging.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:56.580
Begin dive!

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.160
Opening main tanks!

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:03.370
Engine operation normal.
Connecting propulsion units.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.350
Tanks normal. Pressure, okay.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:19.810
All controls are go.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.730
Dive angle, twenty-five degrees.
Depth, thirty meters.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.980
Return ship to horizontal position.
Proceed at minimum speed.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.610
Roger.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:30.990
Prepare detector unit.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:31.360
Aye, Sir.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.330
Sonar screen is operating.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.870
That's the sky over the
Le Mer Straits.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.960
Those reefs are a problem, Sir.
We cannot cut through them.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.340
The airship is increasing speed.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.800
We'll be left behind.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.760
What shall we do, Sir?

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.730
If we go around, we'll lose them.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.600
Let's use that undersea passage.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:06.190
Roger!

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.660
We've reached the reefs. They
measure about 200 meters.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.460
Turn to 2 o'clock.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.290
2 o'clock it is! Steady ahead!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.290
Depth 250 meters.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.670
300 meters...

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.640
Undersea passage is confirmed.
Distance, eighty meters.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:45.520
Entering undersea passage.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:03.580
Up trim plus two degrees.
Steady with the rudder.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.580
Plus two degrees it is, Sir.
Steady ahead.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.970
Vertical clearance, 0.5.
Horizontal clearance, 1.2.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.390
Not much leeway.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.560
Don't worry, we'll make it.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:32.820
Exit visually confirmed.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.320
Distance to exit, twenty meters.

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:40.450
Numerous obstacles barring our way!
I get a metallic reaction!

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.660
Emergency braking action!
Full speed astern!

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.750
Nadia!

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:00.840
Ship at full stop!

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:01.890
No damage taken.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:04.810
What's that?

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.060
Mechanical undersea mines.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.890
So, it was a trap.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.020
Helmsman, we shall back out,
and escape.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.610
Roger, moving astern.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.530
I wonder what's happening?

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:24.490
All of a sudden we come to stop,
then we start going backwards.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.600
Lord Gargoyle, we have completed
dropping the mines.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.680
It's my present to them.

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:54.440
Receive them and perish, my
friends on the Nautilus.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.280
Metallic objects detected to the rear!

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:02.450
Full stop! Emergency brakes!

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.530
Emergency brakes! Full power
to the engines!

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.370
What now?!

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.300
Looks like they have us.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.560
Both the entrance and exit are
completely blocked by mines.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.270
Diving suits will be impossible
to use at this depth.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:39.780
That's right, and the working sphere
can't be used in this grotto.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.240
Shall we try blowing them
away with our jets?

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:46.070
No, the extra pressure would
probably set them off.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.030
It's too dangerous.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:53.460
Captain, the current flow is changing.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:54.870
What's that?!

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:13.810
That fiend Gargoyle!

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.480
Lord Gargoyle, you seem to
be enjoying yourself.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:22.650
I like this kind of game very much.

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.780
My message should be reaching
the Nautilus very soon.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.120
Morse signals!

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:31.790
Read it.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.450
Yes!

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:38.790
"My dear friends on the Nautilus,
I hope you appreciate my present."

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:42.300
These mines are a new floating type
that we have developed.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:46.510
We deeply regret that you have
been chosen to test them.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:49.140
The currents will change three hours
and ten minutes from now.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:53.930
You have to clear away the mines
within this time, Nemo.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:57.100
A word of advice to an old friend.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:58.900
Those mines have been designed

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:04.110
to explode by contact, magnetic
attraction and pressure.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.200
I shall be praying for you.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:14.290
So, we're guinea pigs.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.830
He is playing with our lives.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.470
The present status of this ship is
as I have just explained.

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:29.930
We have not found an effective
means of escape.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:34.640
If anyone has a good idea, come to
the bridge immediately. Over!

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:36.390
This is terrible!

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.190
We all know that.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:42.360
The problem is how can we get out
in one piece. Right, Hanson?

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.940
Mines that are designed to explode
with any disturbance. Difficult...

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.240
What can we do? What can we do?

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:53.450
Think harder!

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:55.040
I've got it!

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.160
We'll use my lovely Katherine!

00:14:56.950 --> 00:15:01.000
You mean you'll seal up your tank, and
send it to remove the mines?

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:02.040
Yes!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.000
But just you...

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.250
Don't worry about that.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.800
Just a minute!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.720
Seniorita, the Gratan is my invention!

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.550
Anywhere it goes, I go too! Right?

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.100
Count me in too.

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:20.940
You two realize you might be killed?

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:25.690
I'm a sorcerer when it comes
to using the magic hands.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.650
Driving Katherine is my job.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.580
You two are the most! I don't
know what to say!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:38.080
You'll let us try, Captain Nemo?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:45.000
All right! I want to help too!
Take me with you!

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.000
You're crazy!

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.260
You stay behind, and
take care of Nadia!

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.800
These jobs have to be
done by grown-ups.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.930
All right! All right! Just like that!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.930
All the way down!

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:01.890
Now, listen, Sanson.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:07.900
We've got to do a good job. We'll
show them how good we are, okay?

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.320
You don't have to tell us that.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:13.030
Actually you want to make an
impression on Nemo, right?

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.700
That's enough, Sanson!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.950
You're a good guy when you aren't
shooting your mouth...

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:30.960
Our mademoiselle is so hardheaded.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.380
This was the only way.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:38.100
On such a dangerous mission, just
the two of us are enough.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:42.060
If we do a good job,
we save this ship,

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.270
and save Grandis too.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:52.070
This is the Nautilus.
Can you hear me?

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.400
Roger, roger, we hear you.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.990
The undersea telephone
is working perfectly.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.700
What happened to Grandis?

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:03.210
Her? Oh, we left her on the ship.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.630
I see. Good.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:11.000
There are only four mines barring our
path that you need to remove.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.510
We only have twenty minutes left.
Hurry it up.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.550
Roger!

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:18.100
Hanson!

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.100
Here we go!

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.980
Got it! Start climbing!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.910
The engine is gasping.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:41.540
Hanson, open up the air cylinder a bit!

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.660
How can I? I've got my hands
full right now!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.750
Okay, it's open. Is this enough?

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.340
Yeah, thanks.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:54.010
Jean!

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.260
Hey, you!

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.720
When did you get on?!

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.560
Shall we take him back?

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:03.470
No, there's no time.

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:07.440
Please let me help! I know
how serious this is.

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.690
I want to do my bit too!

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:12.860
We may not get out of
this alive, you know?

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.190
But you intend to, don't you?

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:17.650
Okay, you'll do.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.280
Gratan to Nautilus.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:21.410
What is it?

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.990
We've picked up an extra member.

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:26.250
The mike, the mike?
Where's the microphone?

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.290
Hey! Cut that out!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.830
Test, test! Test!

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.210
This is Jean!

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:34.250
Nadia, can you hear me?

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.800
I'll be back in a jiffy.
Let's not fight anymore, okay?

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:37.420
Jean...

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:39.130
There she goes!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.470
One mine gone!

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.260
Those guys, leaving me behind!

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.390
There we go!

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:48.230
All right, that's the second one!

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:52.560
There's no problem too
big for us to handle.

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.690
Let's get the next one.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:56.150
Right! Here we go!

00:18:56.150 --> 00:19:00.110
Hanson, watch the oil pressure!
It's going into the red range!

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:05.370
The water pressure is greater
than I expected.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:12.960
That's it. Hang on to it.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:17.050
What?! Damn, the camera's
gone on the blink!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:21.300
The current has stopped. It will begin
flowing the other way soon.

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:22.510
What can we do?

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:25.260
Think! There must be something
we can do!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.600
What's the matter with you?!

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:28.810
Senorita!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:33.360
From now on, just follow
my instructions, okay?!

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:34.480
Right!

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:37.070
Jean! Jean! Can you hear me?

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:38.400
Nadia!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:39.240
Jean...

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:41.990
Oh, Jean...

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.320
I'm sorry.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.490
It's okay. Don't worry.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:49.540
Are you ready?

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.750
Okay, we're waiting!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.000
Keep it straight ahead. That's right.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.500
Now!

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:58.210
A bit to the right. Now straight ahead.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:01.680
That's it. Steady... Steady...

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.640
Now grab it!

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.260
That went real well.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.310
Now proceed straight
ahead thirty meters!

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.360
Good. To the right, five degrees!

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:17.190
A bit more to the right. The right!

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.690
Oops!

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.110
Now, let's get the last one!

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:24.570
We're with you!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.700
The oil pressure is steadily rising!
Is it okay?

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:34.290
I made this Gratan.
Of course it's okay!

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:36.960
You're doing good. Straight ahead!

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.380
Ten meters... five... brake!

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:42.170
Extend the arm. Right.
Not that way!

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:44.300
A bit more to the left. Now right.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.970
Good, now extend the arm.
Extend it a little more!

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.140
No! Too much! Bring it back some.

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:53.350
Right! Just hold that position,
and go forward slowly.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.190
That's it, that's it. A little more!

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:58.270
A little more. Right...

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:00.650
A little more. Get ready...
get ready...

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.490
Now! Grab it!

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:04.740
We're losing pressure!

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:06.240
Shut off the red valve!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:06.910
Right!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:08.580
We're in trouble!

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:09.910
Grab it!

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:14.080
Got it! That's the last one. Hang on!

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:14.870
We got it!

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.540
Good, now push it straight ahead.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:18.250
Right!

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:19.960
Time's almost up.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:21.840
Slow speed astern.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.050
We'll be through in another
thirty meters.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:34.640
It's starting to crack open!

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.940
Sanson! Hanson! Watch out!

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:41.110
This way, you'll hit us with the mine!

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:43.820
We're trying! We've got the
engines fully open!

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:46.030
Looks like engines 2 and 3 are dead!

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:46.490
What?!

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:54.330
The Gratan is coming toward us!
It's on a collision course!

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.920
What're you doing?! Hurry up
and get rid of the mine!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.380
Damn, it won't budge!

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:01.340
All hands, brace for impact!

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:03.960
Sanson! Hanson!

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:05.840
Jean! Please answer me! Jean!

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:10.850
All together!

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:16.180
Contact with the Gratan!

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:17.520
We've escaped from the grotto!

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:19.650
Engines, full speed! Vertical climb!

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:25.740
Jean!

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:06.070
Take off that space titanium.
That's it.

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:06.860
Okay...

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:10.110
The deck feels hot.

00:23:10.110 --> 00:23:13.160
If we can feel that, it means
we're still alive.

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:15.240
We got out alive.

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:21.790
I never thought Grandis would
forgive us with one slap.

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:24.710
She was crying as she slapped us.

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:27.090
Nadia was crying too.

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:30.220
Well, Jean, how do you
feel about all this?

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:33.010
I think I really hate mines now!
